        367.8226318359375,
        384.6263732910156,
        374.8044738769531
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "According to conformal prediction theory, see Shafer and Vovk (2008); Angelopoulos and",
      "bbox": [
        90.0,
        399.1750793457031,
        522.0658569335938,
        408.86236572265625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Bates (2021), a new i.i.d sample xN+1 satisfies",
      "bbox": [
        90.0,
        408.76605224609375,
        313.1885681152344,
        422.412353515625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "P",
      "bbox": [
        236.50198364257812,
        444.8851623535156,
        243.16744995117188,
        449.9469909667969
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "\u0012",
      "bbox": [
        244.9869842529297,
        434.1286315917969,
        253.01608276367188,
        441.1104736328125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "xN+1 ∈C",
      "bbox": [
        253.0179901123047,
        437.2601623535156,
        300.2290344238281,
        452.0633544921875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "i",
      "bbox": [
        304.0830078125,
        435.6565246582031,
        306.7490234375,
        440.96466064453125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "N",
      "bbox": [
        302.2019958496094,
        442.04052734375,
        307.9823303222656,
        447.3486633300781
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "D",
      "bbox": [
        300.2259826660156,
        447.4034118652344,
        306.77740478515625,
        454.92718505859375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "\u0013",
      "bbox": [
        310.3219909667969,
        434.12860107421875,
        318.35107421875,
        441.1104431152344
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "≥1 −i+1",
      "bbox": [
        321.3819885253906,
        440.1197204589844,
        368.92242431640625,
        452.0633239746094
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "N+1.",
      "bbox": [
        352.8810119628906,
        442.3760986328125,
        375.4997253417969,
        455.25421142578125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "(7)",
      "bbox": [
        508.0610046386719,
        442.3760986328125,
        522.0028076171875,
        452.0633850097656
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Note that in (7), the set D is also subject to randomness. In other words, (7) stands on",
      "bbox": [
        90.0,
        471.4151916503906,
        522.0220947265625,
        481.71337890625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "average only if the set D is re-sampled for each xN+1. However, in reachability analysis",
      "bbox": [
        90.0,
        483.65673828125,
        522.025146484375,
        495.26336669921875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "and data-driven applications more generally, we may be restricted to a single, fixed data",
      "bbox": [
        90.0,
        499.1250915527344,
        522.0438842773438,
        508.8123779296875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "set D. Therefore, we need to take into account the probability on the left hand side of (7),",
      "bbox": [
        90.0,
        512.0631713867188,
        522.0633544921875,
        522.3613891601562
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "conditioned on the sample D.",
      "bbox": [
        90.0,
        525.6122436523438,
        230.90272521972656,
        535.9104614257812
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "3.1. Statistical Guarantees",
      "bbox": [
        90.0,
        554.0391235351562,
        236.88015747070312,
        563.7264404296875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "In this section, we ensure statistical independence between the nonconformity function r",
      "bbox": [
        90.0,
        573.34814453125,
        521.6950073242188,
        583.0354614257812
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "and the set D by splitting it into a training set Dtrain and a calibration set Dcal. The use of",
      "bbox": [
        90.00003051757812,
        586.2861938476562,
        521.9981689453125,
        598.221435546875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "distinct sets of samples from the same measurement (i.e., a training set and a calibration",
      "bbox": [
        90.00003051757812,
        600.4461059570312,
        522.0111694335938,
        610.1334228515625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "set) is essential to ensure the independence of the samples used for computing the p-values",
      "bbox": [
        90.00003051757812,
        613.99609375,
        522.0003051757812,
        623.6834106445312
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "and conformal regions from the nonconformity function, which is computed based on the",
      "bbox": [
        90.00003051757812,
        627.5451049804688,
        522.0658569335938,
        637.232421875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "training set, see Angelopoulos and Bates (2021) and Bates et al. (2023). This is a special case",
      "bbox": [
        90.00003051757812,
        641.0941162109375,
        521.9894409179688,
        650.7814331054688
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "of conformal prediction called split conformal prediction or inductive conformal prediction.",
      "bbox": [
        90.00003051757812,
        654.64306640625,
        522.0875854492188,
        664.3303833007812
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The computational advantage of this method lies in its requirement to fit the model only",
      "bbox": [
        90.00003051757812,
        668.1920776367188,
        522.0439453125,
        677.87939453125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "once. However, this comes at the cost of statistical efficiency as the method necessitates the",
      "bbox": [
        90.00003051757812,
        681.7420654296875,
        521.9457397460938,
        691.4293823242188
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "division of the data into separate, and therefore smaller, training and calibration data sets.",
      "bbox": [
        90.00003051757812,
        695.2910766601562,
        522.07666015625,
        704.9783935546875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "7",
      "bbox": [
        303.509033203125,
        725.8359375,
        308.4903259277344,
        734.6827392578125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    }
